WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.650
March 15   14:00

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.980
We've been climbing forever.
Aren't we there yet?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.900
You're so impatient. It's not far now.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.250
You're sure we can learn about Victor's 
past if we go to this Chronos HQ?

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.370
HQ has detailed records of all 
Chronos Rulers it employs.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:29.840
Only thing is...

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.550
I've hidden my darling's records in my room.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.570
What?!

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.610
They're waiting in the highest
 part of the castle,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:40.600
like a princess in a fairy tale.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.140
If you want them back, you have 
to marry me! Okay, darling?

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.610
If I get my memories back,

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.860
it'll prove whether or not 
you're really my wife, right?

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.340
If you are, there's no need
 to marry you again.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.600
We're here! This is the entrance to HQ!

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.570
There's nothing here.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:29.970
Silly. It's a secret organization 
because ordinary people can't find it.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.600
This boulder beneath us is under 
the effects of Slow Down.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.370
Making contact with an 
Oath of Time releases it.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.200
<b>Release</b>

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:44.210
If you're afraid of heights,
you might want to close your eyes.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.470
Oh, so it's underground!

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.380
Yep! Welcome home, darling!

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.090
This is the home base of 
the Chronos Rulers...

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.410
Chronos!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.370
Mina has returned.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.010
It appears she has brought them here,
as she was ordered.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.880
I will now go and receive them.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.740
All as you wish it, Master.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.940
You are Victor and Kiri, yes?

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.260
Welcome to Chronos.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.260
I am Snake, head of the technology division.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.460
No need to be tense! Relax, relax!

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:53.020
Are we not comrades in the 
subjugation of Horologues?

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.520
And Mina...

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.670
You've done fine work.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.420
We have eagerly awaited your return.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:00.270
Huh?

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:01.900
The truth is...

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.530
I wanted to see you in this school uniform!

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.360
This is the summer uniform 
of the famed high school

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:12.160
for girls of nobility,
St. Laurent High School, circa 1987!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.090
The school was closed just 
after it came into use,

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.420
and only a few were preserved, 
making it a legendary find!

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.170
I finally got my hands 
on one for 50,000 euros!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.050
I'm sure it'll look adorable on y—

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.380
I won't give up!

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:33.930
School uniforms have a beauty that 
transcends age and social standing!

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.370
The head of the technology division?

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.240
Don't worry about him.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.470
He's just a perverted old geezer.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:48.010
A perverted old geezer? That hurts.

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.420
This is a matter of course.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.500
I am also a Chronos Ruler,

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.290
and the thing I rule is...

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.750
high school girls' uniforms!

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:10.430
And now that I've given a brief 
introduction of myself...

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.850
I must say, Mr. Victor,
I've heard much about you.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:15.770
You have?

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:20.670
Yes. May I have a look at the scar 
left when the Horologue bit you?

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.730
It's preventing the flow 
of time out of your body!

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.810
This is most definitely the 
original Oath of Time...

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.360
Also known as UNIQUE!

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.820
This is the treasure that we at Chronos 
have sought for a thousand years!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.000
Chronos was established 2,200 years ago.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:45.980
It was formed by gathering the very 
best humans to combat Horologues.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.190
Today, it has grown into a massive family

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:52.090
with a total of 689 personnel 
among all its branches.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.430
Oh?

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:58.070
For having so many people, 
it looks awfully deserted.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:01.440
Everyone just happens to be out and about.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.540
This is where I was a long time ago, right?

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.180
Can you tell me what I was like back then?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.530
I'm afraid I don't know much about that.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.950
I only joined less than ten years ago.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.700
Victor, it's still too risky to 
drop our guard around them.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.210
No one who likes school uniforms can be bad.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:24.830
Oh! Are you like me, Victor?!

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:28.250
Of course. That's how I knew with one look

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:32.390
that this uniform is not from 1987.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.200
Huh?!

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.870
My girlfriend from back in middle school,

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.990
Alice from St. Laurent High School, 
didn't wear a uniform like this.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.910
School uniforms...

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:47.010
Why do you only have clear memories 
of useless things like that?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.260
There was also Lisa from Amelia High School

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.990
and Jill from Feiler Girls' High School...

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.160
How nostalgic.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.120
Those are all legendary girls' high schools!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.320
Do you want their uniforms?

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:02.330
I could arrange that for you.

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.000
Please, sir!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.580
How supremely fortuitous it 
was that I met you this day!

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:11.260
I would like to humbly present 
to you these two uniforms!

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.290
Huh? I do like school uniforms,

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.720
but I like what's found 
inside them much more.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.230
Give those to Kiri. He'll be thrilled.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:20.600
Look, Victor...

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.140
Now, please don't say that. This is...

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:28.320
the mission bestowed upon me by my master.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.030
This is... Slow Down?!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.030
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.830
Didn't I tell you?

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:35.580
I am a Chronos Ruler.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.690
Snake!

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.650
These are the master's orders.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:41.840
The recovery of UNIQUE has been the 
wish of Chronos for a millennium.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.360
I won't stand for that!

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.230
If you take UNIQUE from 
my darling, he'll die!

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.670
I wondered what sort of heroes 
of justice you guys would be.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:55.690
I guess you're really people who'd 
sacrifice others to get your way.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.140
Seventy-six!

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:03.540
That is the number of people 
who remain alive here at HQ.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:24.740
We have sacrificed the 
lives of far too many.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:31.050
But if we have UNIQUE, which is capable 
of ruling the time of all living things,

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.180
we can control the Horologues

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:38.120
and put a swift end to this war,
which has persisted for thousands of years.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.550
And the price for that

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.900
is no more than the life 
of a single man: you!

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:50.010
I believe a sacrifice like
this aligns with justice.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.070
Mina, take care of the rest.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.030
You've done splendidly well.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.360
What are you saying?! 
I won't abandon my darli—

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.390
This is a message from the master.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.180
"Letting personal feelings interfere 
with your duty is intolerable."

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:07.650
Now, bring our two visitors to my lab.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.250
Oh, and be careful not to 
soil the school uniforms.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:15.110
I get it. You don't want to sacrifice 
any more of your comrades.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:18.260
You truly care about the others 
in this organization, don't you?

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.050
But...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.960
It just so happens that I care 
about my partner, too.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:23.890
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.600
If I die, Kiri will cry like a baby.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:32.740
So I cant give you my life just yet.

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:33.880
Kiri, let's go.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:38.280
You were right. It was a bad idea to 
drop our guard around these people.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:44.380
I won't let you escape!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.160
What?!

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.200
Bye-bye.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.860
<i>My darling never believed me
in the first place.</i>

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:03.880
Darling, wait!

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.690
I didn't know what the master had in mind!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.890
I wasn't trying to trick you!
 Please believe me!

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:12.070
If fate sees fit, I'll see you again.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.150
Victor...

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:32.690
You're leaving... again?

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.230
After them! Don't let them escape!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:47.610
Just try and lay one finger on my darling.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.730
I'll kill you all myself!

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.080
Mina! Where are you going?!

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.730
The master will be furious!

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.860
So it turned out to be a trap.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.930
But I never figured they'd try to kill us.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:08.200
In a way, humans are far more 
troublesome than Horologues.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:11.260
But since we don't know what 
sort of hand they're playing,

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.400
retreating for now was a good decision.

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.600
You've gotten much calmer, Victor.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.960
<b>Heh Heh Heh</b>

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:20.920
No!

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:26.280
What are you thinking, Victor?!

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.220
Nothing ventured, nothing gained!

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:30.080
Wait!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:34.510
Oh, have a bath drawn for me at the hotel!

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.010
Hey! Victor!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:41.140
Damn it!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.680
Orders from the master!

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.200
Apprehend Victor Putin, dead or alive!

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.710
He can't have gotten far!

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.600
Split up and find him!

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:53.520
Yes, sir!

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.210
Ding-dong. Correct!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.720
I haven't gotten far.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.910
But if you can't see what's right under 
your nose, you've got a ways to go.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.730
The decoy plan worked.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:10.930
Avoiding battle is an important tactic, too.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.020
Now, as for where my records are...

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.890
If I believe Mina...

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.930
<i>They're in the highest part of the castle,</i>

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:22.690
<i>waiting for the prince to take them away.</i>

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:37.550
Damn it! Where was he 
hiding this many cards?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.120
All the cards were destroyed at once?

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.680
What did this?

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.230
You really hadn't run away yet?

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.940
Seriously, did you think a bunch 
of toys like these would stop me?

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:00.940
Well?

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.910
The master has said we're free 
to kill the card bastard...

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.070
But sadly, he didn't say the same about you.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.140
It's no fun at all!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:14.310
But you're his buddy, right?

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:18.080
So if I torture you, I bet you'll cry out

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.910
and call Victor right to me.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.200
<i>There's an Oath of Time in his gauntlet.</i>

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.370
<i>So he's a Chronos Ruler, too?</i>

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:59.280
<i>His first attack burned up 
all the cards instantly,</i>

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.730
<i>but he fights exclusively with his fists.</i>

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.550
<i>So there are two possibilities...</i>

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.500
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:10.050
<i>One is that he may have a flamethrower 
or similar weapon in his fist.</i>

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.390
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.220
A sword made of water, eh?

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.140
If you control water,
you're just as spineless as you look!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.140
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:23.200
If you're a man, let's see you fight 
me fair and square with your fists!

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.690
<i>If that's the case, I only 
need to avoid his fists.</i>

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.570
Don't you wuss out on me!

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:32.690
You're very simple-minded.

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:37.200
My water drops have already surrounded you.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.200
Speed Up!

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.950
You're the simple-minded one, you idiot!

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:49.630
I'm not picky about how I achieve my goals.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.800
Cheating, deceiving, outwitting...

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.870
I'm a villain to the core, after all.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:56.680
My weapon is not my fist.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.810
It's the fire of explosions!

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.510
I'm the Chronos Ruler of fire, Blaze!

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:04.730
Every manner of flame is my servant.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.720
Even the sparks at your feet,
with my orders,

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:10.640
will become a magnificent blaze 
that burns all to the ground!

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.790
Aw, rats. I reduced him to ashes 
before I could torture him.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:20.620
Oh, well. I just need to find Victor.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.210
The second possibility

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.960
is that your fists are fake,
and you control the flames themselves.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:29.960
In which case, I need to be on the 
lookout for surprise attacks.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:36.800
But if I see them coming and prepare myself,
I have nothing to fear.

00:16:39.030 --> 00:16:41.060
You are indeed a nefarious villain.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:43.850
But the fact that you're so easy to read

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.310
means you're just a rogue 
playing childish tricks.

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.870
Hey, now...

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:52.110
You're a more interesting 
toy than I thought.

00:16:56.340 --> 00:17:00.040
Darling! Darling, where are you?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.870
Please come out!

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:04.630
<i>Where could he be?</i>

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:07.960
<i>Did he really escape to the outside?</i>

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.750
<i>No, Victor was fixated on 
reclaiming the time he's lost.</i>

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.820
<i>He wouldn't give up on it that easily.</i>

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:16.640
It couldn't be...

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.640
This must be it.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.970
It's hardly even guarded at all.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:42.030
A whole room covered in flowers...

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.930
Talk about a super-dreadnought-class romantic.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:01.530
This place is totally mismatched 
with HQ in its design, though.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:23.870
Here it is!

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:25.740
The record of my work from back then!

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:30.930
Huh?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.500
Wh-What language is this?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.010
I can't read this crap!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:47.540
January 6th, 2002...

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.980
Which means this was taken twelve years ago.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:53.440
And it's a picture of me with...

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:54.950
Mina.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:58.180
Was she really my...

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.490
Victor?

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:09.940
Using your sex appeal to get your way?

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.630
That's quite an old-fashioned method.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:14.260
I'm all for honey traps, though.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.640
Want to head straight for the bed?

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:21.610
I finally see you after so long, 
and you're as rude as ever.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.440
After so long?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:36.770
<i>Is she an enemy, or...</i>

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:40.860
<i>At the very least, she doesn't 
have an Oath of Time on her.</i>

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:42.780
<i>A non-combatant?</i>

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:46.190
Would you like tea or something harder?

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.940
Orange juice!

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:55.160
Just who are you, anyway?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.990
How do you know me?

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.170
You really don't remember anything, do you?

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:05.130
Nope. So if you do know, could you tell me?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.060
What really happened twelve years ago?

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:14.020
I did find the record of my work 
for this organization in here.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:19.190
But why did I join this Chronos 
organization in the first place?

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.110
And above all,

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:25.120
how can I get back the time 
that's been taken from me?

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:27.910
You're so impatient.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.620
Don't be in such a rush.
I'll explain everything from the start.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.180
Let's see...

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:38.810
Do you know the origin of "Chronos," 
this organization's name?

00:20:38.810 --> 00:20:39.530
Nope.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:42.530
Chronos is the god of time.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:47.260
He is a being of legend who keeps the 
flow of all the universe's time stable.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.590
Relying on time as his chief sustenance,

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:53.830
he subjugated the demons that 
disturbed the ways of the universe.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.520
Those demons were the Horologues.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:55.520
Those Demons Were the Horologues

00:20:56.420 --> 00:20:58.890
Their battle lasted millions of years,

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:01.530
and ended in Chronos's victory.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:01.530
Ended in Chronos's Victory

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:05.770
But a small number of Horologues survived.

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:09.280
For that reason, Chronos tasked his 
descendants with their elimination.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.280
Tasked His Descendants With Their Elimination

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:13.800
That is why we gather in his name

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.750
and continue to fight the Horologues.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:20.010
That's not what I want 
to hear about, though.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:22.800
For starters, I'm an atheist.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:26.260
We have to brush off the sparks that 
fall on us with our own hands.

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:30.840
If a god exists who can save us,
 I'd like to see his face.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.770
But you've seen one already.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:39.990
I'm saying...

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:45.790
There is a god

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:48.700
standing right in front of you!

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.710
Twilight of the Idols

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:40.190
The Concept of Anxiety
